{
  "$schema": "./permission-vectors.md",
  "version": 1,
  "$comment": [
    "Shared conformance vectors for the capability-certificate permission decision.",
    "",
    "Two implementations must agree on every case here, byte-for-byte including deny",
    "reason strings (docs/PROXY_ARCHITECTURE.md §3.3):",
    "  - TypeScript: packages/trust/src/resolve-permission.ts",
    "      run by packages/trust/__tests__/conformance.test.ts",
    "  - Go:         vaultysclaw-sensor/internal/authz/resolve.go",
    "      run by vaultysclaw-sensor/internal/authz/conformance_test.go",
    "",
    "A vector that passes in one language and fails in the other is a release blocker,",
    "not a test to adjust: two implementations of an authorization function that disagree",
    "are a vulnerability. Add cases here first, then make both sides pass.",
    "",
    "Times are milliseconds since epoch, matching the TypeScript number representation.",
    "`expiresAt` is always present and is either a number or null — never absent.",
    "An absent `resource` on an action means 'no resource', which is NOT the same as an",
    "empty string (see the empty-resource cases below); both are pinned deliberately."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "unscoped active certificate grants the capability",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null
        }
      ],
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "grantingCertId": "c1" }
    },
    {
      "name": "no certificates at all denies",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access" },
      "certs": [],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'internet_access'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "certificate without the requested capability denies",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["api_call", "knowledge_search"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'internet_access'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "expired certificate denies",
      "now": 5000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": 4999
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'internet_access'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "expiresAt exactly equal to now is already expired",
      "now": 5000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": 5000
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'internet_access'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "expiresAt one millisecond in the future still grants",
      "now": 5000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": 5001
        }
      ],
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "grantingCertId": "c1" }
    },
    {
      "name": "revoked certificate denies",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "revoked",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'internet_access'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "superseded certificate denies",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "superseded",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'internet_access'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "scoped certificate matches an exact resource",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access", "resource": "api.openai.com:443" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null,
          "scope": { "resource": "api.openai.com:443" }
        }
      ],
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "grantingCertId": "c1" }
    },
    {
      "name": "scoped certificate denies a different resource",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access", "resource": "evil.example:443" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null,
          "scope": { "resource": "api.openai.com:443" }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'internet_access' for resource 'evil.example:443'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "scoped certificate denies an action carrying no resource",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null,
          "scope": { "resource": "api.openai.com:443" }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'internet_access'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "unscoped certificate matches any resource",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access", "resource": "anything.at.all:443" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null
        }
      ],
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "grantingCertId": "c1" }
    },
    {
      "name": "resourcePattern with a trailing wildcard matches",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "api_call", "resource": "mcp://github/create_issue" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["api_call"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null,
          "scope": { "resourcePattern": "mcp://github/*" }
        }
      ],
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "grantingCertId": "c1" }
    },
    {
      "name": "resourcePattern denies a non-matching resource",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "api_call", "resource": "mcp://gitlab/create_issue" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["api_call"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null,
          "scope": { "resourcePattern": "mcp://github/*" }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'api_call' for resource 'mcp://gitlab/create_issue'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "resourcePattern with several wildcards matches",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "api_call", "resource": "mcp://github/issues/create" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["api_call"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null,
          "scope": { "resourcePattern": "mcp://*/issues/*" }
        }
      ],
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "grantingCertId": "c1" }
    },
    {
      "name": "regex metacharacters in a pattern are matched literally, not as regex",
      "$why": "A '.' in a pattern must not match an arbitrary character — otherwise 'a.b' would authorize 'axb'.",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "api_call", "resource": "mcp://sxrv/tool" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["api_call"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null,
          "scope": { "resourcePattern": "mcp://s.rv/*" }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'api_call' for resource 'mcp://sxrv/tool'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a pattern with no wildcard is an exact match, metacharacters included",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "api_call", "resource": "mcp://s.rv/tool" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["api_call"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null,
          "scope": { "resourcePattern": "mcp://s.rv/tool" }
        }
      ],
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "grantingCertId": "c1" }
    },
    {
      "name": "maxUses exhausted denies",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "api_call", "resource": "mcp://github/create_issue" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["api_call"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null,
          "scope": { "resourcePattern": "mcp://github/*", "maxUses": 2 },
          "usedCount": 2
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'api_call' for resource 'mcp://github/create_issue'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "maxUses not yet reached grants",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "api_call", "resource": "mcp://github/create_issue" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["api_call"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null,
          "scope": { "resourcePattern": "mcp://github/*", "maxUses": 2 },
          "usedCount": 1
        }
      ],
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "grantingCertId": "c1" }
    },
    {
      "name": "absent usedCount is treated as zero",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "api_call", "resource": "mcp://github/create_issue" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["api_call"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null,
          "scope": { "resourcePattern": "mcp://github/*", "maxUses": 1 }
        }
      ],
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "grantingCertId": "c1" }
    },
    {
      "name": "the first usable matching certificate wins",
      "$why": "Pins iteration order: the decision must be stable across implementations, not 'any matching cert'.",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "skipped-revoked",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "revoked",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null
        },
        {
          "id": "skipped-wrong-capability",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["api_call"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null
        },
        {
          "id": "first-match",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null
        },
        {
          "id": "also-matches",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null
        }
      ],
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "grantingCertId": "first-match" }
    },
    {
      "name": "invariant: adding a revoked certificate never grants more access",
      "$why": "packages/trust/CLAUDE.md invariant 1 — must hold in both implementations.",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "system_command" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c-revoked",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["system_command"],
          "status": "revoked",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null
        },
        {
          "id": "c-active-other",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'system_command'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "invariant: adding an unrelated certificate never removes access",
      "$why": "packages/trust/CLAUDE.md invariant 2 — a narrow scoped cert alongside a broad one must not shadow it.",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access", "resource": "api.anthropic.com:443" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c-narrow",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null,
          "scope": { "resource": "api.openai.com:443" }
        },
        {
          "id": "c-broad",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null
        }
      ],
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "grantingCertId": "c-broad" }
    },
    {
      "name": "an empty-string resource takes the short deny message",
      "$why": "The TS reason picks its form with a truthiness check on action.resource, so '' behaves like absent. Pinned so the Go port does not use a nil check and silently diverge.",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access", "resource": "" },
      "certs": [],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'internet_access'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a scoped certificate does not match an empty-string resource",
      "now": 1000,
      "action": { "capability": "internet_access", "resource": "" },
      "certs": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "agentDid": "did:vaultys:proxy",
          "capabilities": ["internet_access"],
          "status": "active",
          "issuedAt": 0,
          "expiresAt": null,
          "scope": { "resource": "api.openai.com:443" }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "allowed": false,
        "reason": "No active certificate grants 'internet_access'"
      }
    }
  ]
}
